 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Timestamps strictly increase across calls. Amounts are positive integers. Levels 1-2 as variant 2. pay(ts,id,amount) withdraws amount if the account exists and holds at least amount, counts it as outgoing, and returns a global sequential id \"payment<N>\" (N counts successful payments from 1), else null. A cashback of floor(2% of amount) is credited to the account at exactly ts+86400000; due cashbacks are applied before any operation whose timestamp is at or after the due time. getPaymentStatus returns \"IN_PROGRESS\" or \"CASHBACK_RECEIVED\", or null if the account is missing or the payment does not exist or does not belong to that account. ",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
